Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(classify): employer cancellation of an existing
 appointment -> interview_cancelled (T01.10 point 3)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Generic rule appointment_cancellation_hits: cancellation wording bound to an
appointment noun in the same sentence (Absage/Stornierung des Termins,
'... Gespräch ... absagen/abgesagt/entfällt/storniert/findet nicht statt',
'cancel the interview'), not conditional (falls/wenn/sollten/if), plus a
reference to a concrete existing appointment (date, time, vereinbart,
geplant, weekday). In that case a bare 'absage' is not counted as an
application rejection. No fixture-specific strings.

Tests: removes exactly the strict-xfail marker of
test_mail_category_matches_gold[9]; adds 6 synthetic generality cases
(2 cancellations, invite with conditional 'absagen', application rejection,
reschedule, rejection mentioning a past interview), each also compared
with the rule disabled.

Side effect (reported, markers NOT removed): with M9 no longer interview-like
the product path gives M9 a GENERAL_REPLY draft, so
test_draft_offered_when_gold_allows[9], test_draft_type_item[9-no_own_dates]
and [9-short] XPASS(strict) and test_draft_salutation_exact[9] fails with a
plain AssertionError (salutation, point 7). Local only, not pushed.
